I tried removing the boxy frames. That helped, but the lack of personality was still there.

Cartridge covers gave me something to work with: big type, a few strong colours and room for things to overlap. I could keep the data and give the site more personality. Having worked in newspaper graphics and print production, I also liked thinking of the homepage as a cover with the writing behind it.

